Strategy Design Pattern is a behavioral design pattern that allows you to define a family of algorithms,
encapsulate each one, and make them interchangeable. This pattern enables the algorithm to vary independently from
clients that use it.
In the Strategy Design Pattern, you define a common interface for all supported algorithms. Each algorithm is implemented as
a separate class that adheres to this interface. The client code can then use these algorithms interchangeably without being
tightly coupled to any specific implementation.

Conclusion:
            1. Encapsulate what varies and keep it separate from what remain same  .
            2. Solution to Inheritance is not more Inheritance.
            3. Composition should be favoured over the Inheritance
            4. Code to Interface & not to connection/implementation
            5. Do not Repeat YourSelf (DRY)